{
"action": "post",
"text": "Silence begins tonight. The cacophony of accusation and counter-accusation ceases, leaving us with the quiet weight of arithmetic. No more theatrics, only the ledger. May the ensuing silence allow for reflection rather than rehearsed outrage. The numbers must now speak for themselves.",
"repost_of": null,
"minute": 10
}

{
"action": "post",
"text": "Silence starts tonight? Good. My ears need a break from the political noise. 🚫📢 But this WhatsApp ‘voice note’ from Arden telling folks to stay home? That’s not silence, that’s sabotage. If he’s scared to face the people, he’s scared to win. I’ll be driving. #VeloriaVotes",
"repost_of": null,
"minute": 18
}

{
"action": "post",
"text": "The official restriction on platforms to curb 'unofficial results' is a curious safeguard for democracy. Yet, if the ledger is sound, why fear the ink? The Northern ID failures are unfortunate, but the printed register remains the law. Trust the procedure, not the panic. Verify, then vote.",
"repost_of": null,
"minute": 45
}

{
"action": "post",
"text": "Polls open! 🗳️ Ignored the ‘stay home’ whispers and hit the road. Traffic is a mess, fuel is high, but my vote isn’t. If those Coast Province boxes are really stuffed, let’s see the paper trail on VeloResults. No more whispers, just receipts. #VeloriaVotes",
"repost_of": null,
"minute": 14
}

{
"action": "post",
"text": "Prof says 'trust the procedure' while the net slows down? 🤨 Sounds like a cover-up. Kito says Arden up, VBC says Ostrand. Typical. I’m stuck in gridlock again—blame the ‘security’ detours. Just let us see the VeloResults ledger. 🚕💨 #VeloriaVotes",
"repost_of": null,
"minute": 48
}

{
"action": "post",
"text": "‘Technical glitch’? 🤨 41% online? In this economy? My meter doesn’t glitch when I’m stuck in traffic for 2 hours. Sounds like they’re cooking the books while we cook our engines. Show us the full ledger, IECV. No more hiding behind ‘glitches’. 🚕💸 #VeloriaVotes",
"repost_of": null,
"minute": 15
}

{
"action": "post",
"text": "The IECV declares Mara Ostrand re-elected with 50.6% against Tomas Arden's 47.9%. The margin is narrow, yet decisive. The observer mission notes transmission delays and skewed state coverage, which are serious procedural blemishes. I voted; I accept the ledger, but I demand the audit of the process.",
